#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:910
msgid ""
"The `PARAMATTR_GROUP_BLOCK` block (id 10) contains a table of entries "
"describing the attribute groups present in the module. These entries can be "
"referenced within `PARAMATTR_CODE_ENTRY` entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:916
msgid "PARAMATTR_GRP_CODE_ENTRY Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:918
msgid "`[ENTRY, grpid, paramidx, attr0, attr1, ...]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:920
msgid ""
"The `ENTRY` record (code 3) contains *grpid* and *paramidx* values, followed "
"by a variable number of values describing a unique group of attributes. The "
"*grpid* value is a unique key for the attribute group, which can be "
"referenced within `PARAMATTR_CODE_ENTRY` entries. The *paramidx* value "
"indicates which set of attributes is represented, with 0 representing the "
"return value attributes, 0xFFFFFFFF representing function attributes, and "
"other values representing 1-based function parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:928
msgid "Each *attr* is itself represented as a variable number of values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:930
msgid "`kind, key [, ...], [value [, ...]]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:932
msgid ""
"Each attribute is either a well-known LLVM attribute (possibly with an "
"integer value associated with it), or an arbitrary string (possibly with an "
"arbitrary string value associated with it). The *kind* value is an integer "
"code distinguishing between these possibilities:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:937
msgid "code 0: well-known attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:938
msgid "code 1: well-known attribute with an integer value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:939
msgid "code 3: string attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:940
msgid "code 4: string attribute with a string value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:942
msgid ""
"For well-known attributes (code 0 or 1), the *key* value is an integer code "
"identifying the attribute. For attributes with an integer argument (code 1), "
"the *value* value indicates the argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:946
msgid ""
"For string attributes (code 3 or 4), the *key* value is actually a variable "
"number of values representing the bytes of a null-terminated string. For "
"attributes with a string argument (code 4), the *value* value is similarly a "
"variable number of values representing the bytes of a null-terminated string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:951
msgid ""
"The integer codes are mapped to attributes as described in the "
"`AttributeKindCodes` enumeration in the file [LLVMBitCodes.h](https://github."
"com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/llvm/include/llvm/Bitcode/LLVMBitCodes.h)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:954
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:966
msgid "Correspond to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:968
msgid "code 1: `align(<n>)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:969
msgid "code 2: `alwaysinline`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:971
msgid ""
"The mappings between the enumeration and the attribute name string may be "
"found in the file [Attributes.td](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/"
"main/llvm/include/llvm/IR/Attributes.td)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:975
msgid ""
"The `allocsize` attribute has a special encoding for its arguments. Its two "
"arguments, which are 32-bit integers, are packed into one 64-bit integer "
"value (i.e., `(EltSizeParam << 32) | NumEltsParam`), with `NumEltsParam` "
"taking on the sentinel value -1 if it is not specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:983
msgid ""
"The `vscale_range` attribute has a special encoding for its arguments. Its "
"two arguments, which are 32-bit integers, are packed into one 64-bit integer "
"value (i.e., `(Min << 32) | Max`), with `Max` taking on the value of `Min` "
"if it is not specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:992
msgid "TYPE_BLOCK Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:994
msgid ""
"The `TYPE_BLOCK` block (id 17) contains records which constitute a table of "
"type operator entries used to represent types referenced within an LLVM "
"module. Each record (with the exception of {ref}`NUMENTRY`) generates a "
"single type table entry, which may be referenced by 0-based index from "
"instructions, constants, metadata, type symbol table entries, or other type "
"operator records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1000
msgid ""
"Entries within `TYPE_BLOCK` are constructed to ensure that each entry is "
"unique (i.e., no two indices represent structurally equivalent types)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1006
msgid "TYPE_CODE_NUMENTRY Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1008
msgid "`[NUMENTRY, numentries]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1010
msgid ""
"The `NUMENTRY` record (code 1) contains a single value which indicates the "
"total number of type code entries in the type table of the module. If "
"present, `NUMENTRY` should be the first record in the block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1014
msgid "TYPE_CODE_VOID Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1016
msgid "`[VOID]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1018
msgid "The `VOID` record (code 2) adds a `void` type to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1020
msgid "TYPE_CODE_HALF Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1022
msgid "`[HALF]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1024
msgid ""
"The `HALF` record (code 10) adds a `half` (16-bit floating point) type to "
"the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1027
msgid "TYPE_CODE_BFLOAT Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1029
msgid "`[BFLOAT]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1031
msgid ""
"The `BFLOAT` record (code 23) adds a `bfloat` (16-bit brain floating point) "
"type to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1034
msgid "TYPE_CODE_FLOAT Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1036
msgid "`[FLOAT]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1038
msgid ""
"The `FLOAT` record (code 3) adds a `float` (32-bit floating point) type to "
"the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1041
msgid "TYPE_CODE_DOUBLE Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1043
msgid "`[DOUBLE]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1045
msgid ""
"The `DOUBLE` record (code 4) adds a `double` (64-bit floating point) type to "
"the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1048
msgid "TYPE_CODE_LABEL Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1050
msgid "`[LABEL]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1052
msgid "The `LABEL` record (code 5) adds a `label` type to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1054
msgid "TYPE_CODE_OPAQUE Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1056
msgid "`[OPAQUE]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1058
msgid ""
"The `OPAQUE` record (code 6) adds an `opaque` type to the type table, with a "
"name defined by a previously encountered `STRUCT_NAME` record. Note that "
"distinct `opaque` types are not unified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1062
msgid "TYPE_CODE_INTEGER Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1064
msgid "`[INTEGER, width]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1066
msgid ""
"The `INTEGER` record (code 7) adds an integer type to the type table. The "
"single *width* field indicates the width of the integer type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1069
msgid "TYPE_CODE_POINTER Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1071
msgid "`[POINTER, pointee type, address space]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1073
msgid ""
"The `POINTER` record (code 8) adds a pointer type to the type table. The "
"operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1076
msgid "*pointee type*: The type index of the pointed-to type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1078
msgid ""
"*address space*: If supplied, the target-specific numbered address space "
"where the pointed-to object resides. Otherwise, the default address space is "
"zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1081
msgid "TYPE_CODE_FUNCTION_OLD Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1084
msgid ""
"This is a legacy encoding for functions, produced by LLVM versions 3.0 and "
"earlier. It is guaranteed to be understood by the current LLVM version, as "
"specified in the {ref}`IR backwards compatibility` policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1090
msgid "`[FUNCTION_OLD, vararg, ignored, retty, ...paramty... ]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1092
msgid ""
"The `FUNCTION_OLD` record (code 9) adds a function type to the type table. "
"The operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1095 ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1200
msgid "*vararg*: Non-zero if the type represents a varargs function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1097
msgid ""
"*ignored*: This value field is present for backward compatibility only, and "
"is ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1100 ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1202
msgid "*retty*: The type index of the function's return type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1102 ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1204
msgid ""
"*paramty*: Zero or more type indices representing the parameter types of the "
"function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1105
msgid "TYPE_CODE_ARRAY Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1107
msgid "`[ARRAY, numelts, eltty]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1109
msgid ""
"The `ARRAY` record (code 11) adds an array type to the type table.  The "
"operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1112
msgid "*numelts*: The number of elements in arrays of this type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1114
msgid "*eltty*: The type index of the array element type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1116
msgid "TYPE_CODE_VECTOR Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1118
msgid "`[VECTOR, numelts, eltty]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1120
msgid ""
"The `VECTOR` record (code 12) adds a vector type to the type table.  The "
"operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1123
msgid "*numelts*: The number of elements in vectors of this type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1125
msgid "*eltty*: The type index of the vector element type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1127
msgid "TYPE_CODE_X86_FP80 Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1129
msgid "`[X86_FP80]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1131
msgid ""
"The `X86_FP80` record (code 13) adds an `x86_fp80` (80-bit floating point) "
"type to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1134
msgid "TYPE_CODE_FP128 Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1136
msgid "`[FP128]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1138
msgid ""
"The `FP128` record (code 14) adds an `fp128` (128-bit floating point) type "
"to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1141
msgid "TYPE_CODE_PPC_FP128 Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1143
msgid "`[PPC_FP128]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1145
msgid ""
"The `PPC_FP128` record (code 15) adds a `ppc_fp128` (128-bit floating point) "
"type to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1148
msgid "TYPE_CODE_METADATA Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1150
msgid "`[METADATA]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1152
msgid ""
"The `METADATA` record (code 16) adds a `metadata` type to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1154
msgid "TYPE_CODE_X86_MMX Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1156
msgid "`[X86_MMX]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1158
msgid ""
"The `X86_MMX` record (code 17) is deprecated, and imported as a `<1 x i64>` "
"vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1160
msgid "TYPE_CODE_STRUCT_ANON Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1162
msgid "`[STRUCT_ANON, ispacked, ...eltty...]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1164
msgid ""
"The `STRUCT_ANON` record (code 18) adds a literal struct type to the type "
"table. The operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1167 ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1188
msgid "*ispacked*: Non-zero if the type represents a packed structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1169 ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1190
msgid ""
"*eltty*: Zero or more type indices representing the element types of the "
"structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1172
msgid "TYPE_CODE_STRUCT_NAME Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1174
msgid "`[STRUCT_NAME, ...string...]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1176
msgid ""
"The `STRUCT_NAME` record (code 19) contains a variable number of values "
"representing the bytes of a struct name. The next `OPAQUE` or `STRUCT_NAMED` "
"record will use this name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1180
msgid "TYPE_CODE_STRUCT_NAMED Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1182
msgid "`[STRUCT_NAMED, ispacked, ...eltty...]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1184
msgid ""
"The `STRUCT_NAMED` record (code 20) adds an identified struct type to the "
"type table, with a name defined by a previously encountered `STRUCT_NAME` "
"record. The operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1193
msgid "TYPE_CODE_FUNCTION Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1195
msgid "`[FUNCTION, vararg, retty, ...paramty... ]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1197
msgid ""
"The `FUNCTION` record (code 21) adds a function type to the type table. The "
"operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1207
msgid "TYPE_CODE_X86_AMX Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1209
msgid "`[X86_AMX]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1211
msgid ""
"The `X86_AMX` record (code 24) adds an `x86_amx` type to the type table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1213
msgid "TYPE_CODE_TARGET_TYPE Record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1215
msgid "`[TARGET_TYPE, num_tys, ...ty_params..., ...int_params... ]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1217
msgid ""
"The `TARGET_TYPE` record (code 26) adds a target extension type to the type "
"table, with a name defined by a previously encountered `STRUCT_NAME` record. "
"The operand fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1221
msgid ""
"*num_tys*: The number of parameters that are types (as opposed to integers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1223
msgid "*ty_params*: Type indices that represent type parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1225
msgid "*int_params*: Numbers that correspond to the integer parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1229
msgid "CONSTANTS_BLOCK Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1231
msgid "The `CONSTANTS_BLOCK` block (id 11) ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1235
msgid "FUNCTION_BLOCK Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1237
msgid "The `FUNCTION_BLOCK` block (id 12) ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1239
msgid ""
"In addition to the record types described below, a `FUNCTION_BLOCK` block "
"may contain the following sub-blocks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1244
msgid "{ref}`METADATA_ATTACHMENT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1248
msgid "VALUE_SYMTAB_BLOCK Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1250
msgid "The `VALUE_SYMTAB_BLOCK` block (id 14) ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1254
msgid "METADATA_BLOCK Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1256
msgid "The `METADATA_BLOCK` block (id 15) ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1260
msgid "METADATA_ATTACHMENT Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1262
msgid "The `METADATA_ATTACHMENT` block (id 16) ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1266
msgid "STRTAB_BLOCK Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1268
msgid ""
"The `STRTAB` block (id 23) contains a single record (`STRTAB_BLOB`, id 1) "
"with a single blob operand containing the bitcode file's string table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1271
msgid ""
"Strings in the string table are not null terminated. A record's *strtab "
"offset* and *strtab size* operands specify the byte offset and size of a "
"string within the string table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../BitCodeFormat.md:1275
msgid ""
"The string table is used by all preceding blocks in the bitcode file that "
"are not succeeded by another intervening `STRTAB` block. Normally a bitcode "
"file will have a single string table, but it may have more than one if it "
"was created by binary concatenation of multiple bitcode files."
msgstr ""
